      "documentSlug": "lighter-zero-fee-perpetuals-and-api",
      "documentConcept": "Lighter zero-fee perpetuals and API",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:4b78b67ef3541093992f4cda4e62798978913f40513dcbd130a690233d75f73c",
      "text": "Lighter is a ZK-rollup perp and spot DEX on Ethereum with a central limit order book. Standard accounts pay 0% maker and taker on regular perp and spot orders; the cost is a 300 ms delay on taker orders, cancels and modifies, and a 60 requests/minute API limit. Plus (0.005%, higher rate limits) and Premium/Advanced (0.004% maker, 0.028% taker, 140 ms, LIT-staking discounts, up to 72,000 sendTx/min) are opt-in via the changeAccountTier endpoint. Trading uses SignerClient-signed sendTx over REST or WebSocket with per-order nonces. Operational risk is real: the Oct 2025 single-sequencer outage, and the 16 Nov 2026 theft of about 10.39M USDC through keys recovered from nonce-reusing custom signing code. Critics call the zero fee a latency tax.",
